Failover Mechanism - 
	Failover is the ability to switch automatically and seamlessly to a reliable backup system. just active-passive approach.
	
automatically switching from a failed primary system to a backup/standby system so the service keeps running with minimal downtime.

Purpose: Improve availability, reliability, and fault tolerance.
How it works: Primary server is monitored using a heartbeat. If the heartbeat stops, the backup takes over.
Failover cluster: Multiple servers/nodes work together. If one fails, another handles its workload.

Two configurations -
	Active - Active , Active - Passive
	
Failover vs Failback:
	Failover: Primary → Backup
	Failback: Backup → Primary after the original system is recovered.
	
